  "body": "## What changed\n- make `daily_offer_quota_reservation.usage_date` the source of truth for quota day attribution whenever a request-id reservation exists\n- prevent an action reserved just before midnight and audited just after midnight from charging both quota days\n- retain audit timestamp day attribution only for legacy audits that predate the reservation ledger\n- add regression coverage for cross-midnight confirmation and same-day audit reconciliation\n\n## Why\nPR #134 made quota request-idempotent and audit-backed, but an audit created after midnight could otherwise be counted in the new day even when its persistent reservation belongs to the previous day. The hard `/25` safety limit must charge each real action exactly once to its reservation day.\n\n## Safety semantics\n- active reservation still counts conservatively\n- CONFIRMED/AMBIGUOUS audits still form a durable floor\n- released/legacy behavior is unchanged\n- no quota slot can migrate to a different day just because audit persistence happens after midnight",
